# Copy to `.env` and pick a target. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so
# keep real tokens out of it.
#
# VITE_HERMES_URL is the dashboard root, including any path prefix the backend
# is served under. VITE_HERMES_TARGET names which of the two installs that is,
# and vite.config.ts cross-checks the two at startup: a label that disagrees
# with its URL aborts the dev server rather than quietly mislabelling a session.
# Leave the target out and it is derived from the URL.
#
# The app reads the resolved target back as `HERMES_TARGET` from
# `src/modules/core/services/hermes/config.ts`.

# --- The cloud VM -----------------------------------------------------------
# Hermes sits behind Caddy under /dashboard there; the bare host serves an empty
# 200, so the prefix is required. Auth is ungated, and the session token is
# injected into /dashboard/ for the dev server to scrape.
VITE_HERMES_URL=https://vm-8ky5zqjqcj3t.imaginecloud.app/dashboard
VITE_HERMES_TARGET=vm

# --- A local dashboard ------------------------------------------------------
# Confirm which install holds the port before trusting it:
#   curl -s http://127.0.0.1:9121/api/status | jq .computer_home
# VITE_HERMES_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9121
# VITE_HERMES_TARGET=local

# Optional. Aborts startup when the backend reports a different COMPUTER_HOME,
# turning "somebody else's roster" into an error. Note it also aborts when the
# backend is simply unreachable.
# VITE_HERMES_COMPUTER_HOME=/root/.computer

# Not read by this app — kept for manual curl against the VM.
# CLOUD_HERMES_TOKEN=
